# Tolerant fixture: a quoted key (Appendix C.2.7). A key is a bare name (6.1), so
# quoting one is a validity error under the strict grammar; the tolerant reader
# removes the quotes, reports a `name-quote` repair, and then applies the ordinary
# key rules unchanged.
#
# The three spellings are deliberate: double quotes, single quotes, and the `=`
# separator. What the relaxation must NOT do is widen anything - the word between
# the quotes still has to be a legal key for the scope it sits in, so this file
# carries no unknown key and no key from another scope.
# `quoted-unknown-key.zh-CN.cliff` is the counter-example that must stay refused.
#
# Expected under `--tolerant`: THREE repairs, all `name-quote` (the `namespace`
# line, the group `context` line, and the entry `max-width` line) - and nothing
# else. `cliff-test/tests/clarion/test_read_modes.py` asserts exactly this, and
# `tests/fixtures/README.md` records it.
CLIFF 1.1
"namespace": demo
clan: quoted-key
source-language: en-US
target-language: zh-CN

[video]
'context': "Video settings screen."
type: label

<resolution>
source: "Resolution"
target: "分辨率"
status: final
"max-width" = 12
